h each other and their thermodynamic ideal. Exergy efficiency is defined for a device as: "]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 25.9, "y": 71.4, "width": 40.7, "height": 7.8, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 25.9, "y": 71.4, "width": 40.7, "height": 7.8, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["equation"]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 25.9, "y": 71.4, "width": 40.7, "height": 7.8, "rotation": 0, "text": ["$$\n\\epsilon = { \\frac { \\mathrm { e x e r g y o u t p u t } } { \\mathrm { e x e r g y i n p u t } } } = { \\frac { \\mathrm { w o r k ~ o u t p u t } } { { \\mathrm { m a x i m u m p o s s i b l e } } { \\mathrm { w o r k } } { \\mathrm { o u t p u t } } } }\n$$"]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 26.1, "y": 80.7, "width": 46.6, "height": 10.3, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 26.1, "y": 80.7, "width": 46.6, "height": 10.3, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 26.1, "y": 80.7, "width": 46.6, "height": 10.3, "rotation": 0, "text": ["By definition, the theoretical limit of exergy efficienc